# 2026-07-23 23:01:06.243230
+Good. Now implement server2.py.
+
+Only edit server2.py. Do not edit server1.py or rest_test.py.
+
+Requirements:
+1. Connect to Cassandra.
+2. Set session.default_consistency_level = ConsistencyLevel.TWO.
+3. Create keyspaces prod and test using SimpleStrategy with replication_factor 3.
+4. Create table stocks_by_ticker in both keyspaces:
+   ticker text,
+   date date,
+   name text static,
+   sector text static,
+   high double,
+   low double,
+   PRIMARY KEY (ticker, date)
+
+5. Implement the same six Flask routes as server1.py:
+   POST /<db>/api/companies/<ticker>
+   POST /<db>/api/companies/<ticker>/records/<date>
+   GET /<db>/api/companies/<ticker>/records
+   GET /<db>/api/companies/<ticker>/records/<date>
+   GET /<db>/api/companies/<ticker>/records/range
+   GET /<db>/api/companies/<ticker>/records/monthly
+
+6. Return the same JSON shapes and status codes as server1.py.
+7. For monthly averages, fetch all rows for the ticker and compute averages in Python.
+8. For missing data, return {"error": "not found"} with status 404 like server1.py.
+9. Use fully qualified keyspace.table names in queries, like test.stocks_by_ticker.
+10. Keep code simple and close to server1.py.
+
+After editing, suggest the commands to rebuild server2 and run pytest in the server2 container.

